A||||4||Adrift||Changing seat belt color?||||1||
Z||000000||Adrift||11-12-2001||12:22 AM||||I'd like to change the color of my seat belts from khaki to black. What's the best way to do this? (I used the search feature and couldn't find anything)||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||11-12-2001||05:44 AM||||A strong solution of Ritt dye. May have to do it a couple of times. Its good for changing to darker, but wont work for making them lighter. Experiment on a spot at the inner part of belt first. Some nylons in belts wont take dye very well.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||11-12-2001||12:59 PM||||Rit might work but will probably be temporary. It's not UV stable. Rit is also known to bleed out. If you get in the car wet it could transfer to your cloths. <P>You have to be very carefull what you treat that material with... The nylon is tough but certain chemicals could damage it and leave it too weak to hold you in a wreck.<P>I don't know what you're doing to you interior, but another choice might be to install the grey belts. Not black but they may go better for you than the tan.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Adrift||11-12-2001||01:01 PM||||Ogre- How would I be able to get a pair of grey belts? It is against the law to sell belts from wrecking yards...||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||11-12-2001||04:49 PM||||You can get them if you watch Ebay. Lisa got her gray ones there, and sold her tan ones to pay for them.||||reg||1
